{n}You hear Nurah's voice ring out from behind him,{/n} "You know the truth, that wasn' the Lady of the Sun, it was a demon and she's been tricking your people. If {mf|he|she} was really a demon, {mf|he|she} could have easily broken your arm already and your practice sword would do nothing."
{n}The man turns his head to look at Nurah before quickly turning back to you.{/n} "No, that can't be right. If we were being tricked, then what about those other demons? They weren't demons? Oh Lady of the Sun, what have we done? What can I do now?"
{n}You hear Nurah once again.{/n} "You'll have to figure out what to do on your own. But lashing out at random people isn't going to help." {n}The man drops the wooden sword before running off. Nurah saunters towards you.{/n} "Oh do not give me that 'I'm so proud of you' look. I just didn't want to listen to you whine about me killing him. I was not talking about myself." {n}She averts her eyes from your gaze.{/n} "Anyways, I need to go report what my boss probably already knows. Try to avoid getting impaled by any dangerous wooden swords without me around to save you." {n}Nurah walks off with a wave.{/n}

{n}You hear Nurah's voice ring out from behind him,{/n} "So, what made you think that jumping between two demons was a good idea?"
{n}The man turns his head towards Nurah while stammering.{/n} "T-t-two?"
{n}Nurah's voice continues,{/n} "Yeah two. Did you really think that a demon would be talking to a random person you've never seen before out of sight? Wouldn't it make more sense for a demon to be talking to another demon?" {n}The man quickly looks between the two of you.{/n} "Of course there is no telling who else is a demon here. We could have replaced anyone..." {n}The man's eyes widen as he drops the sword and runs away screaming.{/n}
{n}Nurah saunters towards you.{/n} "Oh that was some great fun. I bet he'll be halfway to Cheliax before he stops screaming. Well it has been a pleasure Commander, but I need to go report what my boss probably already knows. Try to avoid getting impaled by any dangerous wooden swords without me around to save you." {n}Nurah walks off with a wave.{/n}

{n}Nurah stretches her arms above her head.{/n} "Nope, just make sure you win in the Midnight Fane. I'd hate to lose such an entertaining partner in crime."
{n}She walks away from you, when suddenly a loud crash ruins the farewell. As both of you turn to the source of the sound you see a young man staggering towards Nurah. While the young man is dressed in regal clothes, they hang loose on his emaciated frame. The young man gracelessly falls to his knees before Nurah, although you aren't sure whether this was deliberate or if his spindly legs simply gave out.{/n}
"Please! You have to help me! I have earned my master's displeasure. I don't know what my mistake was, but he refuses to grant me any meals. I don't know what he plans for me, but I fear for my life. I beg for your mercy!" {n}Tears begin to fall from his face onto Nurah's feet. From this angle, you are unable to see Nurah's reaction to the young man's words.{/n}

{n}You groan as you get up. You aren't sure how much time passed, but you imagine long enough that people are going to wonder what you were doing. As you begin to redress, you find a note next to your clothes.{/n}
"I have some things I need to take care of, but I'll see you back in Drezen soon."
{n}The note is signed with a kiss.{/n}

"Meet me at the tavern."
{n}Those were the only words that were written on the paper that was handed to you. With those simple words, you set off to the Half Measure. Upon entering, you quickly spot Nurah nursing a mug sitting by herself. A few moments after you enter, she waves you over.{/n}
{n}As you join her at her table, she begins to speak.{/n} "Commander, thanks for joining me."

"E-excuse me? I'm not marrying that drunk if that is what you are suggesting."
{n}You grab some silverware from a nearby table transforming it into a beautiful crown with your mythic power. After placing the crown upon Nurah's head, you whistle drawing the attention of King Thaberdine. You explain to him how you found his long lost daughter.{/n}
"Eh my daughter? I don't remember having a daughter. Wait is that why she's long lost? I forgot where I placed her?" {n}He breaks out into a laugh and is quickly joined by his entourage.
As the laughter dies down, the various members of his "court" begin calling out in a chaotic cacophony,{/n} "She has his eyes!" "No his ears!" "She has his chin!" {n}Thaberdine gets up and takes a close look at her, causing himself to go cross eyed in the process. Having gotten a good look at her, he turns to his companions.{/n} "You are all right! She is the spitting image of me! And she has a family crown too! A round of drinks for Princess... whatever her name is!" {n}The court breaks out in cheers as they drain another pint.
Sensing an opportunity, Nurah approaches her "father" to speak.{/n} "Umm dad, I was thinking, perhaps I should take over the boring duties of ruling while you keep doing the important stuff like drinking and holding court in the tavern. And maybe we could call me queen too."
{n}King Thaberdine gives Nurah a giant smile with the foam from his beer still on his face.{/n} "Of course pumpkin. Did you all hear that? Three cheers for my daughter Queen Pumpkin!" {n}The bar breaks out in cheers{/n}

"I'm not sure I'm the best source on that topic as I'm a warrior, not a scholar, but I'll give it a shot." {n}Targona clears her throat.{/n}
"Angels are born from the purified souls of those who receive their eternal rewards in the Upper Planes. We serve in the eternal war against evil not because we must, but because we want to help others and save them from their suffering... or at least that is how I view it."
{n}She casts her eyes down.{/n} "Unlike mortals, our souls and body are almost inseparable, which is why this corrupt wing is so concerning. It doesn't just risk poisoning my body, but my soul itself."

{n}The complete joy is apparent on her face as soon as the cream touches her tongue. She consumes the first bite with the urgency of a man deprived of water for a week.{/n} "I need to thank them for finding the recipe, it wasn't just like I remembered, but it was still delicious!"
{n}Aivu hops onto the table.{/n} "Delicious? Let me have some!"
{n}With a sweet smile Targona gives Aivu a fork full of cream.{/n} "So sweet!" {n}Aivu begins running around the bar seemingly having gotten a sugar rush from a single bite.{/n}

"And I have the same feelings of love that she has for you. Really, I wish I could just kiss you right now and forget all about this nonsense."
{n}Targona looks at her wing.{/n} "Now I'm wondering if there is some succubus in this wing."
"Probably," {n}is the response from the shadow.{/n}

{n}Targona looks down to her shadow.{/n} "I'll let you have this one Anograt." {n}As she speaks, the shadow reverts to normal.{/n} "Oh thank you!" {n}Targona proceeds to give you a passionate kiss while wrapping her wings around you for a full body hug.
As she eventually pulls away, you see her shadow moving on its own again.{/n} "Don't worry, I'll be sure to teach Silver that one." {n}You think she tried to wink at you, but you can't make anything out on her shadow face.{/n}
"Now that that is done, I can't take any more time away from your mission. I'll be praying for your return everyday, and we'll have to have a proper date once you're back in Drezen."
{n}The shadow adds, "With both of us!"{/n}

{n}Targona looks down to her shadow.{/n} "I'll let you have this one Anograt." {n}As she speaks, the shadow reverts to normal.{/n} "Oh thank you!" {n}Targona proceeds to give you a passionate kiss while wrapping her wings around you for a full body hug.{/n}
{n}As she eventually pulls away, you see her shadow moving on its own again.{/n} "Don't worry, I'll be sure to teach Silver that one." {n}You think she tried to wink at you, but you can't make anything out on her shadow face.{/n}
"Now that that is done, back to work we go. We'll have to have a proper date once we're back in Drezen."
{n}The shadow adds,{/n} "With both of us!"

{n}Targona smiles at you seductively while taking hold of your hand.{/n} "Let's go back to your room. I want to talk with you about something in private and then..." {n}She leaves the thought unfinished, but there is no doubt in your mind what she is thinking.{/n}
{n}Hand in hand the two of you exit the Half Measure. Targona pulls you in for another kiss before the two of you make your way back to your room.{/n}
{n}As the two of you arrive, Targona sits on the bed while smiling at you.{/n} "You know when we first met, I could see the Light of Heaven was tied to your soul. I spent a lot of time worrying whether my feelings for you were somehow caused by that or were a result of the corruption in my wing. Despite all of our connections, I probably would never have acted on those feelings if you hadn't kept reaching out to me. And now that we are together? I am happy beyond belief that you did! I wouldn't be who I am now without you!"

{n}Ruth gets out of her chair to give you a salute once again.{/n} "Commander, I have to thank you for everything you've done."
{n}Targona stands up to bow as well.{/n} "And you have my thanks as well! I promise to do my best to make sure your flank is protected in the final battle."
{n}Anograt just waves at you from the table with a smile.{/n}

{n}As Storyteller returns the scale to your hand, something goes wrong. First you notice your vision going black, but you quickly realize that it isn't just your vision, all of your senses are gone. Silence and darkness, these are the only accompaniments to your thoughts.{/n}
{n}Time seems to lose all meaning in the endless darkness that surrounds you. It is impossible to tell whether you've been here for minutes, hours, or days as the emptiness seems to stretch out to infinity. And then the silence is broken.{/n}
"Please stop, I don't know who you are or why you are doing this, but I can't take this anymore..." {n}In this endless darkness, you can't tell where the voice came from, but soon you hear the speaker once more as she screams out in pain. And then silence falls once again.{/n}

"I wish I could say that I will follow you out of here and escape, but if you used my scale to reach here then it sounds like you are projecting your consciousness to my location rather than physically traveling here, so I doubt I can follow you when you leave. Could you please return to speak to me on occasion? I swear that I won't lose to this darkness. Just like you didn't lose to that wound."
{n}A gasp echoes in the darkness.{/n} "Wait, I do remember you, {name}. I met you before my fight against Deskari. You had an unnatural wound from a demonic attack. Why did I suddenly remember that? Could it be that talking to you is helping me to piece my memories together? If so, I hope to see you again, so we can have some more conversations."
{n}You open your eyes and find yourself back where you started holding the silver scale.{/n}

{n}Focusing your energy into the scale again, you feel your surroundings shifting once more. As you open your eyes, you find yourself not in the wilderness of your last visit, but in a city under an open nighttime sky. Slowly a realization dawns on you as you take in your surroundings. This city is Kenabres, but you can tell that something is wrong. There is no damage from Deskari's attack. Rather, the city looks practically pristine. And perhaps more unsettling, there is no one around. There are no guards shuffling about on night patrol, no sounds of revelry from nearby taverns open late into the night, and no drunks stumbling on their way home. Just...{/n}{n}
silence.{/n}
{n} As you begin to contemplate the possible implications, the silence is finally broken as you hear the flapping of draconic wings from overhead. The silver dragon illuminated by the moonlight lands nearby before transforming into the familiar form of Terendelev to approach you.{/n} "I knew it would be only a matter of time before you would arrive {name}. Whatever happened here is too big for the Crusade to ignore."

"You changed the timeline? But why would I remember the original timeline then? If this was a ploy, then the mastermind wouldn't make that mistake. Couldn't make that mistake!" {n}Her eyes widen as a realization hits her.{/n} "You said that you communicate with me via one of my scales. I assume you had it on you when you traveled through time? Then I think I have an idea of what is happening."
{n}As she takes a moment to compose herself, the black fog ceases its advance, and begins to thin.{/n}
"I think my soul was sundered. Probably by that darkness that you found me in. I think you unintentionally dragged what was left of my soul and bound it to my scale. My memory has been shattered because a part of my soul is still in that darkness. I remember the original timeline because you unintentionally carried this portion of my soul with you when you changed history."
{n}She lets out a deep breath as the dark fog completely vanishes behind her.{/n} "I'm going to need to spend some time thinking about this, but thank you for not giving up on me. I don't know if there is any way to fix this, but hopefully we can find one." {n}She gives you a soft smile as you feel yourself returning to reality. You open your eyes and find yourself back where you started holding the silver scale.{/n}

"I feel like the common thread in these discussions is that I'm missing memories where I would have reason to feel fear, doubt, and other negative emotions. So I only have Terendelev's positive emotions and memories? But then what happened to her... my? Negative memories?"
{n}As she takes a moment to compose herself, the black fog ceases its advance, and begins to thin.{/n}
"I think my soul was sundered. Probably by that darkness that you found me in. I think you unintentionally dragged what was left of my soul and bound it to my scale. My memory has been shattered because a part of my soul is still in that darkness."
{n}She lets out a deep breath as the dark fog completely vanishes behind her.{/n} "I'm going to need to spend some time thinking about this, but thank you for not giving up on me. I don't know if there is any way to fix this, but hopefully we can find one." {n}She gives you a soft smile as you feel yourself returning to reality. You open your eyes and find yourself back where you started holding the silver scale.{/n}

{n}You stare at the draconic skull that was trying to kill you just moments ago. The missing vertebrae in the skeleton makes it clear that this was Terendelev's body reanimated by the demons. As you begin to ponder what this means for the Terendelev that you have come to know, you feel your senses beginning to fade away. You briefly notice the scale shining brightly before your surroundings completely disappear.{/n}
{n}As you regain your senses, you recognize your surroundings. You are in Kenabres again, but it is no longer the peaceful Kenabres of the last time you used the scale. Now it is the Kenabres on the day the demons invaded. Walls are destroyed, buildings are on fire, and you can see a pool of blood in the place where Deskari cut off Terendelev's head.{/n}
{n}Circling in the sky and occasionally roaring is the Ravener made of Terendelev's body. As you are looking around, you spot Terendelev in her human form nearby motioning for you to get over as she takes cover behind the remnants of a collapsed wall. She speaks as you join her behind cover.{/n} "So I have good news and bad news. Good news, my memory seems to be restoring itself. Bad news..." {n}She waves her arm towards the sky that is choked by smoke.{/n}

{n}Ignoring the Ravener, you turn your attention solely to Terendelev. You call upon your mastery over death. The magic that bound Terendelev to her scale is rudimentary at best, an accident caused by the mixture of multiple spells. You overwrite the magic with a proper binding spell. As the magic becomes set, chains spring out from the ground grabbing Terendelev's limbs. She turns to you and glares.{/n} "You're a monster. This goes against the natural order! There is no difference between you and the demons."
{n}Unable to move her arms, she spits at your feet.{/n} "I don't know what you think you are going to accomplish, but I refuse to cooperate." {n}The chains drag her down below the ground as the magic finishes binding her.{/n}
{n}You look up to the Ravener in the sky. With Terendelev properly bound and unable to be stolen from you, the ravener seems to have lost interest. The skeletal dragon redirects itself out of the city ruins, perhaps fleeing to the River of Souls. You open your eyes to see yourself back in Iz.{/n}

{n}You focus your mythic power into the scale. Almost as soon as you begin channeling the energy, you find yourself robbed of your senses again. The endless darkness surrounds you once more. You attempt to begin your search for the voice, but it is impossible to tell if you are even moving without any senses.{/n}
{n}As you ponder how to proceed, an idea occurs to you. If mythic power brought you here, perhaps it can help you as well. And so you bring your power to bear. There is no immediate change in your sight, but you can slowly feel your other senses returning for the darkness surrounding you has been dyed in your power. As you begin to gain your bearings, you hear a sob as a voice cries out.{/n} "No, not more darkness! Get away!"
{n}You blink as you find yourself back in reality. You look down to find that the scale has darkened and shattered. You briefly try and focus on the remnants before determining that the scale no longer works.{/n}

{n}You open your eyes, and see Aranka opening her eyes too. Both of you seem unmoved from where you were at the beginning of this adventure. Aranka's hand is still outstretched to pass you the Compass. The only thing that seems to have changed is that the weight of the compass is missing from your hand.{/n}
{n}Aranka pulls her hand back. Her face contorts in confusion as she notices the absence of the compass.{/n} "What happened to it? I can't imagine it was designed to vanish after a single use..."
{n}As Aranka begins to move around to see where the compass might have fallen, your eye is drawn to a blue butterfly tattoo on the back of Aranka's hand. In addition to you not remembering it being there before, the blue butterfly is so bright you could swear that it is glowing.{/n}

{n}As you close your eyes to go to sleep, you feel a gentle pull beckoning you forth. The pull gradually gets stronger until it becomes irresistible. You don't know where you are being pulled, but you can feel a kind warmth as you get closer to your destination.{/n}
{n}Soon you can tell you have arrived. Opening your eyes, you find yourself seated in the front row of an empty theater. While you don't recognize the theater, you can tell it was built to house grand performances based on the size of the stage and the quality of the furnishings that include rich carpeting, silk coverings, and gilded candelabras.{/n}
{n}Upon the stage is Aranka singing in a language that you don't recognize. She is so engrossed in her song that she hasn't noticed your sudden appearance.{/n}

{n}Once again, you feel the familiar gentle pull of the Compass of Dreams. As the pull draws you closer and closer, you can hear a warm sound getting louder and louder too. It isn't long until you recognize the sound as Aranka's singing.{/n}
{n}Opening your eyes, you appear to be in a dream once more. In front of you is an ivy covered old mill with doodles drawn all across its face. Lying in front of the old mill is a shaggy horse. As you look around for Aranka, you spot her sitting atop the highest blade of the unmoving mill.{/n}
{n}As you approach the mill, Aranka seems to notice you as she waves while she finishes a song.{/n} "Welcome to my special place. I used to come out here for adventures, but it has been a while since I was last here."

{n}Alluring Reverie beams as she claps her hands together.{/n} "It was amazing! Aranka managed to save me from a most foul villain!"
{n}Aranka grimaces.{/n} "I told you it wasn't that big of a deal."
{n}Alluring Reverie flutters her wings causing her to hop off the ground.{/n} "Nothing? You saved my life. Now I have to tell {name} all about it!" {n}Alluring Reverie waves her hand causing three dolls to form from the sand on the beach. One of the dolls, you quickly recognize as Aranka, comes up to the real version's waist. Another doll, which you recognize as Alluring Reverie, is the same height as Aranka. The final doll is about as tall as the Aranka doll, is dressed all in white, and is adorned in golden jewelry.{/n}

"I know you are busy, but you have to make some time for fun too or else you are going to overwork yourself. And then where will the army be?" {n}She pokes you on the nose.{/n} "I'll let you go for now, but don't think I'm going to let my {mf|boyfriend|girlfriend} work themselves to death."
"Regarding the Compass of Dreams, I guess you don't need the extra magic, but if you ever figure out how to get it to work, I'll gladly teach you everything that Alluring Reverie taught me."
{n}Aranka heads to the door to the war room and blows you a kiss before departing.{/n}

{n}Aranka returns the kiss and starts urgently peeling your clothes off. The two of you spend several hours up on the ramparts enjoying each other's company and occasionally avoiding a guard patrol. Eventually, the two of you sneak back into your room falling to sleep in your bed.{/n}
{n}Several hours later you are awoken by Aranka opening the door.{/n} "Oh sorry, did I wake you? I was hoping to let you rest a bit longer." {n}She smiles at you.{/n} "You just get some more rest. Bard's orders!"
"Oh, and if you ever get the Compass of Dreams to work, let me know and I'll teach you everything that Alluring Reverie taught me." {n}Aranka blows you a kiss before slipping out the door.{/n}

{n}Making your way through the city, Minagho transforms into a human form to alleviate suspicion as the two of you make your way to the Sword of Valor. The few guards with the enchantments to pierce her illusion are calmed by your assurances that you are addressing the ghost problem. Standing over the banner, Minagho looks down.{/n}
"It is funny, this artifact is meant to deny demons their freedom on the battlefield, but now it is going to be granting me my freedom..." {n}She wipes a fresh trail from her face, and holds a bloody finger over the edge. A few seconds later, a drop of blood falls landing on the banner. Immediately, Minagho doubles over and curls up as the power flows into her. She bites her lip to stop herself from yelling as pain wracks her body. She remains curled up on the ground for some time before unsteadily moving to get back on her feet. She glares at you as she does so.{/n} "That was a trickle of your power?"
{n}As she rises, her face brightens as she begins to recognize that the pain from the brand is gone.{/n} "Well at least it worked. I would have been pissed if I went through that additional pain for nothing."
